{"type":"assistant","uuid":"4dccf1e0-4c3b-491a-9d51-ad8e985c9c01","session_id":"c7a204af-c61f-459d-824a-738681cb7566","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"id":"4dccf1e0-4c3b-491a-9d51-ad8e985c9c01","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The fix is complete. Here's a summary:\n\n## Bug Analysis\n\n**Root Cause:** `ConcurrentModificationException` in `FileArrayAdapter.java` at `initUI()` (lines 164-170).\n\nThe code iterates over `activity.getFileOpContext().getSecond()` (a collection) to check which files are already selected. Inside this loop, `checkBox.setChecked(true)` is called, which triggers the `OnCheckedChangeListener` callback. That callback then calls `activity.getFileOpContext().getSecond().add(f)` — **modifying the collection while it's being iterated**, causing the crash.\n\nThis happens specifically when quickly toggling checkboxes because `getView()` is called repeatedly during list recycling, and programmatically setting checkbox state fires the listener.\n\n## Fix\n\nThe fix disables the `OnCheckedChangeListener` before programmatically setting the checkbox state, then re-enables it afterward. This prevents the callback from being triggered during iteration:\n\n```java\n// Before: checkBox.setChecked(true) triggered listener → add(f) → ConcurrentModificationException\n// After:  setListener(null) → setChecked(true) → setListener(original)\n```\n\n## Output\n\n- **Patch file:** `patch.patch`\n- **Build status:** BUILD SUCCESSFUL"}],"stop_reason":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":37883,"output_tokens":284,"cache_read_input_tokens":32448,"total_tokens":38167}}}
